-- title:
--   Hecke stability of the toric m-torsion of J₀(N₀p)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, nonzero, and not dividing $N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that the image of $p$ lies in `A.nonunits`. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`, that is, a structure section $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` restricting to the generic point along `barPt A`, a scheme $X$ over `base p` with a relative group law $L$ for `baseRing p`, and bijections identifying `JZero N₀` with the sections of $X$ over the generic point and `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` with the sections over the residue point; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`, i.e. $X \to$ `base p` is an abelian scheme with commutative group law, the two bijections are additive, the generic one is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees mod $\ell$ when the relevant inputs hold, and each Hecke element acts through an $L$-homomorphic endomorphism of $X$. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, and let $m > 0$. Then, for the module structure `heckeModuleBar (N₀ * p)` of the Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[x_q : q \text{ prime}]$ on `JZero (N₀ * p)`, the subgroup `O.toricPts m` — the subgroup of `JZero (N₀ * p)` generated by the range of `O.toricPoint m hm` — satisfies $t \cdot x \in$ `O.toricPts m` for every $t \in$ `HeckeAlg` and every $x \in$ `O.toricPts m`.
--
--   This is the statement that the toric $m$-torsion inside $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, as cut out by the Néron object $O$ at $p$, is a Hecke submodule. It supplies the Hecke-stability datum used in the construction of the ordinary toric data at $p$ and in the subsequent analysis of Hecke generators acting on toric points.
